      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-293568",
      ":question/problem": "In a soccer tournament, the reigning champions score a median of $5$ goals per game in the first seven games. A list showing the total number of goals scored by last year's runners-up over the first seven games is shown below:\n$3, 4, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. Last year's runners-up scored a median of $5$ goals per game over the first seven games.\n2. The median number of goals scored per game over the first seven games are equal for both teams.\n3. A comparison of the medians suggests that the champions score more goals per game overall.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
